  ordered record of "what changed, when, by whom" from day one, notifications become a comparatively cheap consumer of
  that stream, and so does an activity feed, an audit log, or undo. If tasks just mutate state in place, you end up
  diffing or bolting on triggers later, which is the version people regret.

  So: sub-project one is tasks with a change log. Sub-project two is subscriptions and delivery. We'd spec the first one
  now, and I'd keep the notification requirements in view while doing it — as the consumer the event shape has to serve
  — without specifying delivery yet.

  One fact decides whether that's right, and it's the one I can't infer from an empty page.

